WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.142
Four misconceptions are worth removing early.

00:00:03.142 --> 00:00:09.027
An L L M is not a database, attention is not the same thing as reasoning,

00:00:09.027 --> 00:00:17.672
temperature does not make a model more intelligent, and a larger model is not automatically the best model for every

00:00:17.672 --> 00:00:21.662
application. These misconceptions cause real design mistakes.

00:00:21.662 --> 00:00:29.342
For example, treating an L L M like a database can lead someone to trust a fluent answer that was never retrieved from a

00:00:29.342 --> 00:00:30.951
verified source.
